module src::project::serialization::project_item_serialization;

// Port frontier for project_item_serialization.rs — upstream implements
// `SerializableProjectFile` for `ProjectItem`: save creates the item's
// directory (`fs::create_dir`) and writes pretty JSON; load refuses
// directories/missing paths and reads JSON back, clearing
// `has_unsaved_changes` on success.
//
// Both impls are downstream of the serde_json-equivalent project-file
// codec — no ordinary Omega package provides that text-format reader or
// writer today (PORTING.md: an unavailable library facility is a named
// blocker, not a placeholder). The machines land with the codec leg
// recorded on the port board (TASKS.md PROJECT-SERIALIZATION row); the
// filesystem walks themselves (`Filesystem::exists`, `create_dir`,
// `create`/`open`) are portable and ride along in that leg.
